==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|enm}} {{term|discernen}} < {{etyl|fro}} {{term|discerner}} < {{etyl|la}} {{term|discernere||to separate, divide, distinguish, discern}} < {{term|dis-||apart}} + {{term|cernere||to separate}}; see [[certain]].

===Pronunciation===
''(modern pronunciation)''
* {{a|RP}} {{IPA|/dɪˈsɜːn/}}, {{SAMPA|/dI"s3:n/}}
* {{a|GenAm}} {{IPA|/dɪˈsɝn/}}, {{SAMPA|/dI"s3`n/}}

''(older pronunciation)''
* {{a|RP}} {{IPA|/dɪˈzɜːn/}}, {{SAMPA|/dI"z3:n/}}
* {{a|GenAm}} {{IPA|/dɪˈzɝn/}}, {{SAMPA|/dI"z3`n/}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{transitive}} To [[detect]] with the [[sense]]s, especially with the [[eye]]s.
# {{transitive}} To [[perceive]], [[recognize]], or [[comprehend]] with the [[mind]]; to [[descry]].
# {{transitive}} To [[distinguish]] something as being [[different]] from something else; to [[differentiate]].
#: ''He was too young to '''discern''' right from wrong.''
# {{intransitive}} To [[perceive]] [[difference]]s.

====Derived terms====
* [[discernible]]
* [[discernment]]
* [[indiscernible]]

